    "notes": "Revenue: FY2022 onward is restated continuing operations (ex US/Canada architectural, ex silicas); FY2021 and earlier is as originally reported, so the 5-year CAGR mixes bases and the 3-year (0.55%) is the cleaner read. EPS 3-year CAGR (17%) starts from a FY2022 trough ($4.34, raw-material squeeze) and the FY2025 $6.96 includes discontinued items; adjusted EPS fell slightly in FY2025 ($7.58). Owner-FCF series (reported FCF - SBC - est. equity-award taxes): FY2020 $1,765M, FY2022 $429M (working-capital build), FY2025 $1,102M; FCF CAGRs swing on working capital and the FY2024-25 capex step-up and are not a usable growth signal. SBC is ~0.3% of revenue and is not growing faster than cash flow."
